{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/177782-harvesting-honor","id":177782,"title":"Harvesting Honor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-23T03:16:10-07:00","id":177782,"title":"Harvesting Honor","content":"So, Directional Courts. Specifically the West Court and their 'emotion'. I know the flavor text tries to convince us that honor is an emotion, but frankly I'm not convinced. I doubt the child enduring a beating from a father silently is actually feeling particularly honored/honorable. Not to mention that most of the time honor is about how other people percieve it and not actual emotion felt by the person, so essentially the changeling is harvesting their own emotions when looking at people performing honorable deeds. (which is impossible) <br /> <br /> I suppose you can argue for 'stubborness' or 'determination' being the operative emotion, in the sense of &quot;I will do what I need to do and damn the consequences&quot;, but those don't strike me as 'emotions' in the strictest sense either. <br /> <br /> I would like to be convinced, honestly, but I just don't see it at the moment. Did anyone use some other emotion as West primary in their chronicle, and if so, what was it? Or can anyone take me through the mental acrobatics needed to see honor as a thing that can be harvested for glamor? How/where would you even harvest honor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T06:33:33-07:00","id":177881,"title":"","content":"In chasing some words through a couple dictionaries, what I see is that Honor equates to Esteem, and as you point out, it has a lot to do with a community respect that does not seem to be an emotion at all.<br /> <br /> But take it another step, what is the emotion of esteem? I suggest that you are talking about belief in yourself. Almost the opposite of despair. However, it can be a narrow Belief. Your Belief may be tied to a very specific thing, in recognition of just how you have gained Honor in the eyes of everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T19:41:03-07:00","id":178544,"title":"","content":"I'd almost translate it &quot;pride,&quot; if it was me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T02:10:27-07:00","id":180541,"title":"","content":"Well yes, and my problem is that people that perform honorable acts don't often actually 'feel' honor or pride or belief in themselves. The woman that walks into the cold to die because she 'tainted herself with another man' is probably not feeling the 'opposite of despair'. Not to mention that people can feel like they're being honorable while actually behaving without honor at all. What if a man really feels that his honor demands he beats his child for a thoughtless comment? And he feels very righteous beating the child, will then a West courtier standing nearby be able to harvest the honor? What if the West courtier thinks that beating a child is not honorable? What if the person performing an honorable act isn't feeling honorable, but there are people there watching that feel like the person is acting honorably? Depending on answers to these questions Western courtiers either have a REALLY limited supply of glamor or still a REALLY limited supply of glamor with a dose of moral relativism. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where one would even harvest honor, anyway. The only thing I can come up with is martial arts classes, military award ceremonies and court hearings in which the accused is innocent.<br /> <br /> Pride would work better, actually, thank you HobbitGuy. Especially considering the whole 'tiger is the king of all animals' thing Chinese mythology has. I'll think about changing that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T17:27:53-07:00","id":182388,"title":"","content":"I suggest Determination or Resolve. While an individual probably does not feel honor, they my feel determined to achieve a thing, even if that thing is to sacrifice themselves in some way.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I agree that pride seems to fit better with the broader game aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}